To see how this works - look at the 'injection' folder in the 'rooms'
folder of the sample game.

AND if you are seeing this text, you can see that injections can be
nested. So one injection file can contain a reference to another one
(absolute, or relative to the injection file that is pointing to the
other injection file).

And unlike other Elements Injection Elements can be placed anywhere
as long as it's on its own line in your script file. Injections are
handled before any other Element processing is done so you can
place injection Elements inside Message Outputs or other areas that
would normally be problematic.
